{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-72673",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{u}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{{u}^{4}} & = \\\\ {u}^{5}\\cdot {u}^{2-4} & = \\\\ {u}^{5}\\cdot {u}^{-2} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{u}^{5}\\cdot {u}^{-2} & = \\\\ {u}^{5+(-2)} & = \\\\ {u}^{5-2} & = \\\\ {u}^{3} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{u}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{{u}^{4}}={u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
